armGBA-pico patch to upstream armGBA (src/cart/gpio.c, src/gba.h), MPL-2.0 like the files it changes.
Copyright (c) 2026 TheGammaSqueeze. Applied by build.sh to a copy in out/src.

A game may run its rumble motor for only part of a frame, and a frontend that looks at the pin
once a frame then misses it. The writes that leave the motor running are counted where the
frontend can see them, outside struct Gpio so save states keep their layout.

--- a/src/cart/gpio.c
+++ b/src/cart/gpio.c
@@ -216,9 +216,17 @@
 	hw->gyroEdge = !!(hw->pinState & 2);
 }
 
+// The writes since the frontend last looked that left the motor running. A game may run the motor
+// for only part of a frame, so a frontend that looks once a frame counts these rather than taking
+// the pin as the frame ends. Kept outside struct Gpio so save states keep their layout.
+uint32_t gpioRumbleOnWrites;
+
 // Pin 3 runs the motor.
 static void rumbleReadPins(struct GBA* gba) {
 	gba->gpio.rumble = !!(gba->gpio.pinState & 8);
+	if (gba->gpio.rumble) {
+		++gpioRumbleOnWrites;
+	}
 }
 
 // Boktai's sensor: pin 1 resets a counter that pin 0 clocks, and pin 3 reads high once the count
--- a/src/gba.h
+++ b/src/gba.h
@@ -1143,6 +1143,8 @@
 // The tilt sensor, mapped into the save memory's addresses; offset is the address's low 24 bits.
 uint8_t gpioTiltRead(struct GBA*, uint32_t offset);
 void gpioTiltWrite(struct GBA*, uint32_t offset, uint8_t value);
+// Writes that left the rumble motor running since the frontend last cleared this (cart/gpio.c).
+extern uint32_t gpioRumbleOnWrites;
 
 // sio.c
 void sioInit(struct GBA*);
